{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For</b> — The word חרצובות is fourth in the [acrostic] sequence, and in the book of Isaiah: פתח חרצובות רשע (Isaiah 45:1). פתח is like התר (unbinding), and if so, חרצובות is like אגודות (bonds). The meaning: that they ought to have been bound in chains so that He would kill them quickly. R. Moses the Kohen said: כי אין חרצובות עד מותם ואולם הם בריאים — as if written ואולם כל אחד מהם בריא. This is not correct, that the word אולם, which is a word of reasoning, would come last [in the phrase], for it is like לכן, אכן, רק, אך, בלתי, זולתי, למען, בעבור — for thus it is not found in all of Scripture. Others say: כי אולם is missing a כ [i.e., כאולם], and the meaning is: each one is healthy like אולם. And some say: it is missing a ב, and the meaning is: באולם כל אחד בריא — each one is healthy in his אולם." "<b>And the reason for mentioning אולם</b> — that he dwells in a noble house that has an אולם (portico), like the אולם of the House of HaShem mentioned in Chronicles. Or because dwelling in an אולם is healthy for the body, on account of the air that is exposed and there is shade from above. And the correct interpretation in my eyes: after he mentioned the peace of the wicked — I see in their lives and in their death, they die without afflictions and illnesses, plagues and pains, as though their souls have no bonds tied to their bodies." "<b>And אולם</b> — on the pattern of טובם. The meaning: their strength, which is the natural power that guards the body, and it is from the root of יש לאל ידי (1 Samuel 14:6). And the meaning is: they die in their death without toil, and in their lives their natural power is strong and healthy."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {0 "The phrase ובספר ישעיהו introduces the Isaiah citation; the acrostic reference (רביעית, 'fourth') likely concerns the position of חרצובות in the verse of Psalms 73, not in Isaiah. Resolved literally.", 1 "The phrase שלום רשעים refers back to Psalms 73:3 (שלום רשעים); resolved by context rather than explicit citation.", 2 "Ibn Ezra reads אולם here as a noun meaning 'strength/vitality,' deriving it from the root אל (as in יש לאל ידי, 'there is power in my hand'), not as the conjunction 'but.' The phrase על משקל טובם indicates a morphological parallel (pronominal suffix on a noun)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:17.929940626Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}